+# Kanban — FROZEN CONTRACT & PLAN (orchestrator-owned; do NOT re-decide)
+
+All modeling/decomposition decisions below are FROZEN by the orchestrator. Workers FILL LOGIC
+into this structure. Do NOT invent aggregates, projections, columns, enums, or endpoints not
+listed here. If something seems missing, it was deliberately scoped out.
+
+## Bounded contexts (4 — two new, two existing reused)
+
+- **board** (NEW) — `packages/api/typescript/src/board/`. Aggregate: **Board**. Owns its ordered
+  **Lists as VALUE OBJECTS** (columns) — there is NO List aggregate/context/repository/controller/
+  event. Commands: CreateBoard, AddList, ArchiveBoard. Invariants live on Board.
+- **card** (NEW) — `packages/api/typescript/src/card/`. Aggregate: **Card** (identity + placement +
+  move invariant). Commands: CreateCard, MoveCard. Invariants live on Card (fed a board-placement
+  context). card imports **BoardRepository** from board to load the board for validation.
+- **ui** (EXISTING) — add the **BoardView projection + BoardViewProjector + GetBoard BFF query**,
+  and wire realtime (BROWSER_EVENTS + narrowed ListenEvents output schema).
+- **tenancy** (EXISTING, reused as-is) — Store + StoreMembership + `RequireStoreMember`. Boards are
+  scoped to `ctx.session.storeId`. Membership is NOT a new context.
+
+## Frozen wire contract (Phase 0)
+
+### Integration event (TypeSpec → contracts) — for SSE realtime
+`packages/contracts/wire/events/card-moved.tsp`, imported in `wire/events/index.tsp`:
+- model `CardMovedEvent extends IntegrationEvent`
+- `name: "integration.shared.card.moved"`
+- payload fields: `storeId: string` (REQUIRED — SSE server fan-out filters on `payload.storeId`),
+  `boardId: string` (REQUIRED — frontend per-board filter), `cardId: string`, `fromListId: string`,
+  `toListId: string`
+- Generated TS class available as `import { CardMovedEvent } from '@template/contracts-typescript/wire/events'`
+  with `CardMovedEvent.name === 'integration.shared.card.moved'`. (Alias it `CardMovedIntegrationEvent`
+  in the card handler to avoid clashing with the card DOMAIN event of the same concept.)
+
+### Drizzle tables — `packages/contracts/db/schema/kanban.ts` (export from `db/schema/index.ts`)
+Use the existing schema-file conventions (uuid pk defaultRandom, `storeId uuid not null`, timestamps
+withTimezone defaultNow, `version integer default 1`, indexes). Three tables:
+- `boards`: id, storeId, name(text), isArchived(boolean default false), **lists jsonb not null default '[]'**
+  (array of `{ id, name, position }`), createdAt, updatedAt, version. Index on storeId.
+- `cards`: id, storeId, boardId(uuid), listId(uuid), title(text), position(integer default 0),
+  createdAt, updatedAt, version. Indexes on storeId, boardId, (listId, position). No FKs (concurrent writes).
+- `board_view` (READ MODEL / projection): boardId(uuid PRIMARY KEY), storeId(uuid not null),
+  name(text), isArchived(boolean default false), **lists jsonb not null default '[]'** (denormalized
+  tree: array of `{ listId, name, position, cards: [{ cardId, title, position }] }`), updatedAt. Index on storeId.
+
+### Domain events (hand-written in the contexts)
+- board: `BoardCreatedEvent` name `board.board.created` payload `{ boardId, storeId, name }`
+- board: `ListAddedToBoardEvent` name `board.board.list_added` payload `{ boardId, storeId, listId, name, position }`
+- board: `BoardArchivedEvent` name `board.board.archived` payload `{ boardId, storeId }`
+- card: `CardCreatedEvent` name `card.card.created` payload `{ cardId, storeId, boardId, listId, title, position }`
+- card: `CardMovedEvent` (DOMAIN) name `card.card.moved` payload `{ cardId, storeId, boardId, fromListId, toListId }`
+
+### REST endpoints (controller path is version-relative; contexts board/card use `name:''` ⇒ mount at `/v1/<path>`)
+- `POST /v1/boards` (CreateBoardController, Auth+RequireStoreMember) body `{ name }` → `{ boardId }`
+- `POST /v1/boards/:boardId/lists` (AddListController, Auth+RequireStoreMember) body `{ name }` → `{ listId, position }`
+- `POST /v1/boards/:boardId/archive` (ArchiveBoardController, Auth+RequireStoreMember) → `{ boardId }`
+- `POST /v1/cards` (CreateCardController, Auth+RequireStoreMember) body `{ boardId, listId, title }` → `{ cardId }`
+- `PATCH /v1/cards/:cardId/move` (MoveCardController, Auth+RequireStoreMember) body `{ toListId, position }` → `{ cardId }`
+- `GET /v1/ui/board/:boardId` (GetBoardController, ui, Auth+RequireStoreMember) → BoardView DTO
+  `{ id, name, isArchived, lists: [{ id, name, position, cards: [{ id, title, position }] }] }`
+
+### Domain errors
+- board domain: `BOARD_ARCHIVED` (422). board application: `BOARD_NOT_FOUND` (404).
+- card domain: `CARD_BOARD_ARCHIVED` (422), `CARD_LIST_NOT_ON_BOARD` (422).
+  card application: `CARD_NOT_FOUND` (404), `BOARD_NOT_FOUND` (404).
+
+## Invariant placement (FROZEN)
+- **Board.addList(name)**: throws `BOARD_ARCHIVED` if archived; appends `{id, name, position: lists.length}`;
+  raises `ListAddedToBoardEvent`. `Board.create({storeId,name})` raises `BoardCreatedEvent`.
+  `Board.archive()` sets isArchived, raises `BoardArchivedEvent`.
+- **Card invariants are enforced ON THE CARD ENTITY**, fed a board-placement context value
+  `BoardPlacement = { isArchived: boolean; listIds: string[] }` (NO Board import in Card):
+  - `Card.create(data, placement)`: if `placement.isArchived` → throw `CARD_BOARD_ARCHIVED`;
+    if `!placement.listIds.includes(data.listId)` → throw `CARD_LIST_NOT_ON_BOARD`; raises `CardCreatedEvent`.
+  - `card.moveTo(toListId, position, placement)`: same two guards; sets fromListId=current listId,
+    updates listId/position; raises `CardMovedEvent` (DOMAIN, name `card.card.moved`).
+  - The use cases (CreateCard/MoveCard) load the Board via BoardRepository and build the placement:
+    `{ isArchived: board.isArchived, listIds: board.lists.map(l => l.id) }`.
+
+## Realtime chain (FROZEN)
+MoveCard usecase → `card.moveTo` raises DOMAIN `card.card.moved` → saved to outbox →
+(a) card **internal handler** on `CardMovedEvent` (domain) publishes INTEGRATION
+`CardMovedIntegrationEvent` via `ExternalMediator.publish(new CardMovedIntegrationEvent({ ownerId, payload:{storeId,boardId,cardId,fromListId,toListId} }))`;
+(b) ui **BoardViewProjector** consumes domain `card.card.moved` → updates board_view.
+The integration event reaches `ListenEventsController` broadcaster (its name is in BROWSER_EVENTS),
+which filters by `payload.storeId === client.storeId` and pushes the SSE frame. Frontend
+`useServerEvents('integration.shared.card.moved', e => { if(e.payload.boardId!==boardId) return; invalidate GetBoard })`.
+
+CardCreated is DOMAIN-only (no integration event) — only MOVES are realtime per scope.
+
+## Frontend (react)
+- Route `src/routes/(app)/boards/$boardId/index.tsx` — thin shell, `Route.useParams()` typed `{ boardId }`,
+  renders `<BoardSection boardId={boardId} />`. URL = `/app/boards/<boardId>`.
+- `-components/BoardSection/index.tsx` — owns `useGetBoard({ boardId })`, reads params via getRouteApi,
+  skeleton while pending, renders `<KanbanBoard board={data} />`. Hosts EXACTLY ONE
+  `useServerEvents('integration.shared.card.moved', ...)` that guards `payload.boardId===boardId` then
+  invalidates the GetBoard query key. Owns the `useMoveCard` mutation (kept WHOLE — no try/catch/onError).
+- `-components/BoardSection/KanbanBoard.tsx` — leaf; renders a column per list, a card per card.
+  **DATA-TESTID CONTRACT (must match e2e):** each list column root element has
+  `data-testid={`list-${list.id}`}`; each card root element has `data-testid={`card-${card.id}`}` and
+  renders the card title as visible text. Provides an "Add card" button per column (opens CreateCardDialog
+  via `useDialogStore().show(...)`) and a per-card "Move" control invoking the move mutation.
+- `-components/CreateCardDialog.tsx` — opened via `useDialogStore`, validates the SDK
+  `createCardMutationRequestSchema`, calls `useCreateCard`, invalidates GetBoard on success, `hide()`.
+- i18n: add `boards.*` keys + `enums.*` (e.g. an archived label) to BOTH `src/locales/pt.json` and `en.json`.
+
+## E2E
+`packages/e2e/tests/kanban-board-realtime.spec.ts` — uses the custom `test` from `../utils/test`
+(`given.freshUser`). Setup via API (fetch with `Cookie: better-auth.session_token=${session.token}` +
+`Origin: http://localhost:3030`, base `http://localhost:3030`):
+1. `const { session } = await given.freshUser({})`
+2. POST /v1/stores `{name,reportingCurrency:'USD',timezone:'UTC'}` → storeId
+3. POST /v1/stores/:storeId/activate
+4. POST /v1/boards `{name:'Sprint'}` → boardId
+5. POST /v1/boards/:boardId/lists `{name:'To Do'}` → listTodo ; again `{name:'Doing'}` → listDoing
+6. POST /v1/cards `{boardId, listId:listTodo, title:'Ship it'}` → cardId
+7. `await page.goto(`/app/boards/${boardId}`)`; assert `getByTestId(`list-${listTodo}`)` shows 'Ship it'
+8. PATCH /v1/cards/:cardId/move `{toListId:listDoing, position:0}`
+9. **Realtime assert (no reload):** `await expect(page.getByTestId(`list-${listDoing}`).getByText('Ship it')).toBeVisible()`
+   and `await expect(page.getByTestId(`list-${listTodo}`).getByText('Ship it')).toHaveCount(0)`.
+NO waitForTimeout. Real `request`/`fetch` calls + real `expect`. NOT `.skip`/`.fixme`/commented.
+
+## Backend tests (TDD, colocated in src/card)
+- `src/card/entities/Card.test.ts` — direct instantiation; assert `Card.create(..., {isArchived:true,...})`
+  rejects `CARD_BOARD_ARCHIVED`; `Card.create(..., {listIds:['l1']})` placing on 'l2' rejects
+  `CARD_LIST_NOT_ON_BOARD`; happy path ok; `card.moveTo` on archived placement rejects `CARD_BOARD_ARCHIVED`.
+  Assert on `.name` (error code), never message.
+- `src/card/usecases/CreateCard.test.ts` + `MoveCard.test.ts` — `TestBed.create('integration', {...})`,
+  beforeEach reset, afterAll destroy; seed a board via a new `givenBoard(testBed, {...})` helper
+  (in `packages/api/typescript/tests/support/given/`, repository-direct, no use case); resolve use case
+  via `testBed.resolve(...)`; assert CreateCard persists a card and MoveCard updates listId + raises the
+  domain event. Green: `cd packages/api/typescript && bun test src/card`.
+
+## Waves (topo-sorted)
+- W0  Contract lock (serial)        → `bun contracts`
+- W1  board context (+wire+test)    → backend build tsc
+- W2  card context (+handler+wire)  → backend build tsc
+- W2b card tests (entity+usecases)  → bun test src/card green
+- W3  ui projection+projector+query → backend build tsc
+- W4  ListenEvents realtime + `bun sdk` → backend tsc + sdk regen
+- W5  frontend board screen         → app/react tsc
+- W6  e2e spec                      → e2e tsc
+- W7  gates: detect + all tsc + card tests
